import Click from './Click.svelte';

<script>
  const label = "don't click; leverage there's";
</script>

A code span holds `don't`, `there's`, `click` and `leverage`.

```
don't there's click leverage;
```

~~~
don't there's click leverage;
~~~

A link URL is not prose: [the page](https://example.com/click/leverage/dont-there's).

An autolink is not prose: <https://example.com/click/leverage>.

An image URL is not prose: ![Chart](https://example.com/click-leverage.png).

A reference link [holds a URL][ref].

[ref]: https://example.com/click/leverage

A key is not prose: <kbd>click</kbd>, <samp>don't</samp> and <var>there's</var>.

